# Task 148-014: macOS E2E — tmux Backend Full Sprint (GitHub Actions)

## Approach
1. Create `tests/e2e/cross-platform/macos-tmux.test.ts` — 6 tests covering:
   - Platform detection (darwin check)
   - tmux version >= 3.3
   - Mini sprint 3-task lifecycle
   - HB format validation (ISO 8601 + UUID)
   - Result atomic write (kqueue-safe)
   - Cleanup (no orphan tmux sessions)

2. Create `.github/workflows/cross-platform-e2e.yml` — GitHub Actions matrix:
   - macOS + tmux
   - ubuntu + tmux
   - ubuntu + subprocess
   (macOS + subprocess excluded per spec)

3. Create `docs/audits/sprint-148/macos-validation.md` — GO status audit doc

## Files to Create
- tests/e2e/cross-platform/macos-tmux.test.ts (NEW)
- .github/workflows/cross-platform-e2e.yml (NEW)
- docs/audits/sprint-148/macos-validation.md (UPDATE)

## Skip Strategy
- Tests use `describe.skipIf(os.platform() !== 'darwin')` for macOS-specific tests
- tmux availability check for graceful CI skip on envs without tmux
